# Environment template for the SorobanLard Makefile.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (git-ignored) and fill in your values:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   set -a; source .env; set +a
#   make deploy-testnet
#
# The Makefile does not load `.env` by itself, so export the variables
# into your shell first, as shown above.

# Identity used by `stellar contract deploy` in `make deploy-testnet`.
# Must be a key alias known to the Stellar CLI on this machine:
#   stellar keys generate --global my-account --network testnet
#   stellar keys address my-account
#   stellar keys fund my-account --network testnet
# This variable is REQUIRED for `make deploy-testnet`.
STELLAR_ACCOUNT=my-account

# Network the Makefile deploys to. Defined in the Makefile as `testnet`;
# override on the command line, not here, since Make ignores environment
# values for variables it defines itself:
#   make deploy-testnet NETWORK=testnet
#
# NETWORK=testnet

# Contract name used to derive WASM_PATH and WASM_OPT, which `optimize` and
# `deploy-testnet` read. Defined in the Makefile as `sorobanlard`. Override
# it on the command line only if the Wasm file name changes:
#   make deploy-testnet CONTRACT_NAME=sorobanlard
#
# CONTRACT_NAME=sorobanlard

# The RPC URL and network passphrase are NOT read by the Makefile. The
# Stellar CLI resolves them from its own network configuration, which you
# can inspect or set with:
#   stellar network ls
#   stellar network add --global testnet \
#     --rpc-url <RPC_URL> \
#     --network-passphrase "Test SDF Network ; September 2015"
